Package: my-xymon-extensions
Version: @VERSION@-1
Depends: smartmontools, mmc-utils
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: roemer2201 <r.oliver@web.de>
Source: https://github.com/roemer2201/my-xymon-extensions
Description: Portable Xymon client extensions with standalone runner
 Custom monitoring tests for the Xymon systems monitor, bundled with a
 minimal standalone runner (xymon-run.sh) and protocol sender
 (xymon-send.sh) for hosts without a Xymon client, such as
 OpenWrt/TurrisOS routers.
 Included extensions: smart - S.M.A.R.T. disk health monitoring for
 SATA/ATA and NVMe disks, plus eMMC wear/pre-EOL health via mmc-utils;
 temp - all hwmon/thermal temperature sensors (CPU/SoC and switch on
 the Turris Omnia); la - load average with per-core thresholds;
 memory - memory utilization in percent; disk - filesystem usage from
 df in the standard disk column (per-mount thresholds, /dev and /rom
 hidden by default); opkg - pending package
 updates (refreshes the package lists itself, security-relevant
 updates turn red); wifi - Wi-Fi access point metadata via
 iw/ubus/iwinfo (client counts, channel utilization, airtime,
 throughput, TX retries, noise floor; reports clear on routers
 without AP radios); fritzdsl - AVM FRITZ!Box DSL line monitoring via
 TR-064; fritzwan - AVM FRITZ!Box WAN throughput monitoring (both
 need the curl package and stay silent until configured).
